   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv(\"/Users/rkhurana01/Downloads/bgnbd_gamma_model.csv\",index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "2314c746",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Cleaned data shape: (6305, 3)\n",
      "  customer_id transaction_date  monetary_value\n",
      "0       C0001       2023-06-29           50.18\n",
      "1       C0001       2023-07-11           75.82\n",
      "2       C0001       2023-08-22           65.88\n",
      "3       C0001       2023-10-02           95.15\n",
      "4       C0001       2023-12-07           68.19\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Drop missing critical fields\n",
    "df = df.dropna(subset=[\"customer_id\", \"transaction_date\", \"monetary_value\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove duplicate rows\n",
    "df = df.drop_duplicates()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Keep only positive transaction values\n",
    "df = df[df[\"monetary_value\"] > 0]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort for readability\n",
    "df = df.sort_values([\"customer_id\", \"transaction_date\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCleaned data shape:\", df.shape)\n",
    "print(df.head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "2ae1e636",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Customer summary:\n",
      "             frequency  recency      T  monetary_value\n",
      "customer_id                                           \n",
      "C0001              5.0    181.0  185.0         72.4220\n",
      "C0002              5.0    147.0  175.0         64.8380\n",
      "C0003              5.0    128.0  361.0         43.9000\n",
      "C0004              4.0    170.0  337.0        140.8775\n",
      "C0005              1.0    218.0  223.0         31.4800\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 3. GENERATE CUSTOMER SUMMARY METRICS\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "summary = summary_data_from_transaction_data(\n",
    "    df,\n",
    "    customer_id_col=\"customer_id\",\n",
    "    datetime_col=\"transaction_date\",\n",
    "    monetary_value_col=\"monetary_value\",\n",
    "    observation_period_end=df[\"transaction_date\"].max()\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCustomer summary:\")\n",
    "print(summary.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f3a2693e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Convert transactions into customer summary metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "#The `summary_data_from_transaction_data()` function transforms raw transactions into customer-level metrics required by the `lifetimes` models:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **frequency**: number of repeat purchases  \n",
    "- **recency**: time between first and most recent purchase  \n",
    "- **T**: customer age during the observation window  \n",
    "- **monetary_value**: average transaction value for repeat purchases\n",
    "\n",
    "These features form the basis of the BG/NBD and Gamma-Gamma workflow.\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "905f29d5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "BG/NBD input shape: (1000, 4)\n",
      "             frequency  recency      T  monetary_value\n",
      "customer_id                                           \n",
      "C0001              5.0    181.0  185.0         72.4220\n",
      "C0002              5.0    147.0  175.0         64.8380\n",
      "C0003              5.0    128.0  361.0         43.9000\n",
      "C0004              4.0    170.0  337.0        140.8775\n",
      "C0005              1.0    218.0  223.0         31.4800\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 4. FILTER DATA FOR BG/NBD\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "summary_bgnbd = summary[\n",
    "    (summary[\"T\"] > 0) &\n",
    "    (summary[\"recency\"] >= 0) &\n",
    "    (summary[\"frequency\"] >= 0) &\n",
    "    (summary[\"recency\"] <= summary[\"T\"])\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nBG/NBD input shape:\", summary_bgnbd.shape)\n",
    "print(summary_bgnbd.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7eb174f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Fit the BG/NBD model\n",
    "\n",
    "The Beta-Geometric/Negative Binomial Distribution (BG/NBD) model estimates how many purchases a customer is expected to make in the future.\n",
    "\n",
    "In simple terms, it models:\n",
    "\n",
    "- customer purchase frequency\n",
    "- the probability that a customer is still “alive” or active\n",
    "\n",
    "A small penalizer is used to improve numerical stability during fitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "b4a81973",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "BG/NBD model fit complete\n",
      "<lifetimes.BetaGeoFitter: fitted with 1000 subjects, a: 0.00, alpha: 66.10, b: 0.00, r: 1.40>\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 5. FIT BG/NBD MODEL\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "bgf = BetaGeoFitter(penalizer_coef=0.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "bgf.fit(\n",
    "    summary_bgnbd[\"frequency\"],\n",
    "    summary_bgnbd[\"recency\"],\n",
    "    summary_bgnbd[\"T\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nBG/NBD model fit complete\")\n",
    "print(bgf)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1e9048bf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Predict future purchases\n",
    "\n",
    "After fitting BG/NBD, we estimate the expected number of purchases each customer will make in the next 12 time units.\n",
    "\n",
    "This gives the **purchase frequency component** of CLV."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 29,
   "id": "a4013162",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Predicted future purchases:\n",
      "             frequency  recency      T  predicted_purchases_12\n",
      "customer_id                                                   \n",
      "C0001              5.0    181.0  185.0                0.305848\n",
      "C0002              5.0    147.0  175.0                0.318534\n",
      "C0003              5.0    128.0  361.0                0.179813\n",
      "C0004              4.0    170.0  337.0                0.160750\n",
      "C0005              1.0    218.0  223.0                0.099613\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 6. PREDICT FUTURE PURCHASES\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "summary_bgnbd[\"predicted_purchases_12\"] = bgf.predict(\n",
    "    12,\n",
    "    summary_bgnbd[\"frequency\"],\n",
    "    summary_bgnbd[\"recency\"],\n",
    "    summary_bgnbd[\"T\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPredicted future purchases:\")\n",
    "print(summary_bgnbd[[\"frequency\", \"recency\", \"T\", \"predicted_purchases_12\"]].head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e432bc31",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Filter valid rows for Gamma-Gamma\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Gamma-Gamma** model should only be fit on customers who have made at least one repeat purchase and have a positive average monetary value.\n",
    "\n",
    "That is why we keep only rows where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `frequency > 0`\n",
    "- `monetary_value > 0`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "id": "c6357643",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Gamma-Gamma input shape: (999, 5)\n",
      "             frequency  monetary_value\n",
      "customer_id                           \n",
      "C0001              5.0         72.4220\n",
      "C0002              5.0         64.8380\n",
      "C0003              5.0         43.9000\n",
      "C0004              4.0        140.8775\n",
      "C0005              1.0         31.4800\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 7. FILTER DATA FOR GAMMA-GAMMA\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "gg_data = summary_bgnbd[\n",
    "    (summary_bgnbd[\"frequency\"] > 0) &\n",
    "    (summary_bgnbd[\"monetary_value\"] > 0)\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nGamma-Gamma input shape:\", gg_data.shape)\n",
    "print(gg_data[[\"frequency\", \"monetary_value\"]].head())\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "41ca2e97",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 8: Fit the Gamma-Gamma model\n",
    "\n",
    "The Gamma-Gamma model estimates the **expected average transaction value** for repeat customers.\n",
    "\n",
    "This model is commonly paired with BG/NBD because it gives the **monetary component** of CLV."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "02cfe68f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Gamma-Gamma model fit complete\n",
      "<lifetimes.GammaGammaFitter: fitted with 999 subjects, p: 1.12, q: 0.25, v: 1.07>\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 8. FIT GAMMA-GAMMA MODEL\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "ggf = GammaGammaFitter(penalizer_coef=0.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "ggf.fit(\n",
    "    gg_data[\"frequency\"],\n",
    "    gg_data[\"monetary_value\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nGamma-Gamma model fit complete\")\n",
    "print(ggf)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "89d88133",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 10: Predict expected monetary value\n",
    "\n",
    "Once the Gamma-Gamma model is fit, we estimate the expected average purchase value for each eligible customer.\n",
    "This predicted value is more stable than using a single observed transaction amount."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "eed6f992",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Predicted average monetary value:\n",
      "             frequency  monetary_value  predicted_avg_value\n",
      "customer_id                                                \n",
      "C0001              5.0         72.4220            83.924281\n",
      "C0002              5.0         64.8380            75.161685\n",
      "C0003              5.0         43.9000            50.969801\n",
      "C0004              4.0        140.8775           169.672021\n",
      "C0005              1.0         31.4800            99.397144\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 9. PREDICT AVERAGE MONETARY VALUE\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "gg_data[\"predicted_avg_value\"] = ggf.conditional_expected_average_profit(\n",
    "    gg_data[\"frequency\"],\n",
    "    gg_data[\"monetary_value\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPredicted average monetary value:\")\n",
    "print(gg_data[[\"frequency\", \"monetary_value\", \"predicted_avg_value\"]].head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2bc6e79b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 11: Estimate Customer Lifetime Value (CLV)\n",
    "\n",
    "We combine the two model outputs:\n",
    "\n",
    "- predicted future purchases from BG/NBD\n",
    "- predicted average purchase value from Gamma-Gamma\n",
    "\n",
    "A simplified CLV estimate is:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Predicted CLV = Predicted Purchases × Predicted Average Transaction Value**\n",
    "\n",
    "This gives a relative measure of future customer value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "13e3ede9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n",
      "Predicted CLV:\n",
      "             frequency  recency      T  monetary_value  \\\n",
      "customer_id                                              \n",
      "C0001              5.0    181.0  185.0         72.4220   \n",
      "C0002              5.0    147.0  175.0         64.8380   \n",
      "C0003              5.0    128.0  361.0         43.9000   \n",
      "C0004              4.0    170.0  337.0        140.8775   \n",
      "C0005              1.0    218.0  223.0         31.4800   \n",
      "\n",
      "             predicted_purchases_12  predicted_avg_value  predicted_clv  \n",
      "customer_id                                                              \n",
      "C0001                      0.305848            83.924281      25.668071  \n",
      "C0002                      0.318534            75.161685      23.941517  \n",
      "C0003                      0.179813            50.969801       9.165054  \n",
      "C0004                      0.160750           169.672021      27.274765  \n",
      "C0005                      0.099613            99.397144       9.901290  \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# =====================================\n",
    "# 10. ESTIMATE CLV\n",
    "# =====================================\n",
    "\n",
    "gg_data[\"predicted_clv\"] = (\n",
    "    gg_data[\"predicted_purchases_12\"] *\n",
    "    gg_data[\"predicted_avg_value\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nPredicted CLV:\")\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    gg_data[\n",
    "        [\n",
    "            \"frequency\",\n",
    "            \"recency\",\n",
    "            \"T\",\n",
    "            \"monetary_value\",\n",
    "            \"predicted_purchases_12\",\n",
    "            \"predicted_avg_value\",\n",
    "            \"predicted_clv\"\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "    ].head()\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
